  "narrative": {
    "summary": "Qatar governs AI through strategy and guidance led by the Ministry of Communications and Information Technology (MCIT). There is no AI-specific law yet. The National AI Strategy (2019) and the Digital Agenda 2030 set direction; the Artificial Intelligence Committee, established by Cabinet Decision No. 10 of 2021, coordinates implementation. MCIT's ethical AI principles and developer guidelines (2025) form the soft-law core, while binding obligations come from the Personal Data Privacy Protection Law (2016) and, for banks, the Qatar Central Bank's AI Guideline (2024). The next step is a National AI Policy, published as a consultation draft in December 2025, which proposes a central AI policy unit and risk-based oversight of AI used in decisions.",
    "lead_institutions": [
      "Ministry of Communications and Information Technology (MCIT)",
      "Artificial Intelligence Committee",
      "National Cyber Security Agency (NCSA)",
      "Qatar Central Bank (QCB)"
    ],
    "last_deep_review": "2026-10-06",
    "review_notes": "Deep review 2026-10-06. mcit.gov.qa, almeezan.qa and qcb.gov.qa block or fail automated reading; several dates are held at year or month level and flagged in metadata_gaps. Dates were cross-checked only against official pages; news agencies were not used as sources. Sweep: no adoption of the National AI Policy found by 2026-10-06."
  },
